{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YCZ11rHAhzT2WSvGUx1y65","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/structfuse-context/literature_map.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# StructFuse — Related Work Literature Map\\\\n# 最后更新: 2026-05-12\\\\n# 说明: 只收录项目文件中已引用的 + 确定存在的知名论文。不确定的信息标注\\\\\\\"需验证\\\\\\\"。\\\\n\\\\ncategories:\\\\n\\\\n  # ==========================================================================\\\\n  # Category 1: Code Retrieval for Bug Fixing / SWE-bench Ecosystem\\\\n  # ==========================================================================\\\\n  code_retrieval_bug_fixing:\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"SWE-bench 及相关 repo-level 自动修复系统中的代码检索方法\\\\\\\"\\\\n    papers:\\\\n\\\\n      - title: \\\\\\\"SWE-bench: Can Language Models Resolve Real-World GitHub Issues?\\\\\\\"\\\\n        authors: \\\\\\\"Carlos E. Jimenez, John Yang, Alexander Wettig, Shunyu Yao, Kexin Pei, Ofir Press, Karthik Narasimhan\\\\\\\"\\\\n        venue: ICLR\\\\n        year: 2024\\\\n        relation: baseline  # StructFuse 的评估基准\\\\n        summary: \\\\\\\"从 GitHub issues 构建 repo-level bug fixing benchmark，成为自动修复领域标准评估集。\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n      - title: \\\\\\\"SWE-agent: Agent-Computer Interfaces Enable Automated Software Engineering\\\\\\\"\\\\n        authors: \\\\\\\"John Yang, Carlos E. Jimenez, Alexander Wettig, Kilian Lieret, Shunyu Yao, Karthik Narasimhan, Ofir Press\\\\\\\"\\\\n        venue: NeurIPS\\\\n        year: 2024\\\\n        relation: competitor\\\\n        summary: \\\\\\\"基于 LLM agent 的交互式 bug fixing 系统，定义了 ACI 接口范式。\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n      - title: \\\\\\\"AutoCodeRover: Autonomous Program Improvement\\\\\\\"\\\\n        authors: \\\\\\\"Yuntong Zhang, Haifeng Ruan, Zhiyu Fan, Abhik Roychoudhury\\\\\\\"\\\\n        venue: ISSTA\\\\n        year: 2024\\\\n        relation: competitor\\\\n        summary: \\\\\\\"结合代码搜索与 spectrum-based fault localization，利用程序分析缩小修复范围。\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n      - title: \\\\\\\"Agentless: Demystifying LLM-based Software Engineering Agents\\\\\\\"\\\\n        authors: \\\\\\\"Chunqiu Steven Xia, Yinlin Deng, Soren Dunn, Lingming Zhang\\\\\\\"\\\\n        venue: arXiv\\\\n        year: 2024\\\\n        relation: competitor\\\\n        summary: \\\\\\\"无 agent 架构的 two-phase localize-then-repair 方法，在 SWE-bench 上取得强 baseline。\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n      - title: \\\\\\\"SWE-smith: Scaling Data for Software Engineering Agents\\\\\\\"\\\\n        authors: \\\\\\\"John Yang, Carlos E. Jimenez, Alexander Wettig, Karthik Narasimhan, Ofir Press\\\\\\\"\\\\n        venue: arXiv\\\\n        year: 2025\\\\n        relation: building-block  # StructFuse 用其 repo 做数据提取\\\\n        summary: \\\\\\\"自动从 GitHub 生成大规模 SWE-bench 风格训练数据，StructFuse 用其 repos 做 data-flow 提取。\\\\\\\"\\\\n        note: \\\\\\\"需验证 venue（可能已投稿会议）\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n      - title: \\\\\\\"RepoBench: Benchmarking Repository-Level Code Auto-Completion Systems\\\\\\\"\\\\n        authors: \\\\\\\"Tianyang Liu, Canwen Xu, Julian McAuley\\\\\\\"\\\\n        venue: ICLR\\\\n        year: 2024\\\\n        relation: baseline\\\\n        summary: \\\\\\\"Repo-level 代码补全/检索 benchmark，含 RepoBench-R 检索子任务，StructFuse 可用于评估。\\\\\\\"\\\\n        note: \\\\\\\"需验证年份和 venue\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  # ==========================================================================\\\\n  # Category 2: Hard Negative Mining in Contrastive Learning\\\\n  # ==========================================================================\\\\n  hard_negative_mining:\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"对比学习中 hard negative 挖掘策略，以及代码领域的对比学习\\\\\\\"\\\\n    papers:\\\\n\\\\n      - title: \\\\\\\"Dense Passage Retrieval for Open-Domain Question Answering\\\\\\\"\\\\n        authors: \\\\\\\"Vladimir Karpukhin, Barlas Oğuz, Sewon Min, Patrick Lewis, Ledell Wu, Sergey Edunov, Danqi Chen, Wen-tau Yih\\\\\\\"\\\\n        venue: EMNLP\\\\n        year: 2020\\\\n        relation: background\\\\n        summary: \\\\\\\"DPR 开创了 in-batch negatives + BM25 hard negatives 的双塔检索范式，是 StructFuse 对比训练的方法论基础。\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n      - title: \\\\\\\"Approximate Nearest Neighbor Negative Contrastive Learning for Dense Text Retrieval\\\\\\\"\\\\n        authors: \\\\\\\"Lee Xiong, Chenyan Xiong, Ye Li, Kwok-Fung Tang, Jialin Liu, Paul Bennett, Junaid Ahmed, Arnold Overwijk\\\\\\\"\\\\n        venue: ICLR\\\\n        year: 2021\\\\n        relation: background\\\\n        summary: \\\\\\\"ANCE 用 ANN index 动态挖掘 embedding-distance hard negatives，是 StructFuse 的 baseline negative 策略之一。\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n      - title: \\\\\\\"SimCLR: A Simple Framework for Contrastive Learning of Visual Representations\\\\\\\"\\\\n        authors: \\\\\\\"Ting Chen, Simon Kornblith, Mohammad Norouzi, Geoffrey Hinton\\\\\\\"\\\\n        venue: ICML\\\\n        year: 2020\\\\n        relation: background\\\\n        summary: \\\\\\\"视觉对比学习奠基工作，证明 hard negatives 和大 batch size 对对比学习的重要性。\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n      - title: \\\\\\\"Sentence-BERT: Sentence Embeddings using Siamese BERT-Networks\\\\\\\"\\\\n        authors: \\\\\\\"Nils Reimers, Iryna Gurevych\\\\\\\"\\\\n        venue: EMNLP\\\\n        year: 2019\\\\n        relation: background\\\\n        summary: \\\\\\\"Siamese/triplet 网络训练句子嵌入，StructFuse 的对比训练框架与其类似。\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n      - title: \\\\\\\"Mining Hard Negatives with Curriculum for Dense Retrieval\\\\\\\"\\\\n        authors: \\\\\\\"需验证\\\\\\\"\\\\n        venue: \\\\\\\"需验证\\\\\\\"\\\\n        year: \\\\\\\"需验证\\\\\\\"\\\\n        relation: background\\\\n        summary: \\\\\\\"课程学习式 hard negative 挖掘，从易到难训练检索器。\\\\\\\"\\\\n        note: \\\\\\\"需验证完整信息\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  # ==========================================================================\\\\n  # Category 3: Program Analysis for ML\\\\n  # ==========================================================================\\\\n  program_analysis_for_ml:\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"静态分析辅助 ML，结构信息在代码表示学习中的应用\\\\\\\"\\\\n    papers:\\\\n\\\\n      - title: \\\\\\\"CodeQL: Semantic Code Analysis Engine\\\\\\\"\\\\n        authors: \\\\\\\"GitHub / Semmle\\\\\\\"\\\\n        venue: \\\\\\\"Tool (open-source)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        year: 2019\\\\n        relation: building-block  # StructFuse 核心组件\\\\n        summary: \\\\\\\"基于 Datalog 的代码查询引擎，支持 inter-procedural data-flow 分析。StructFuse 用它提取 scope-bounded data-flow graph。\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n      - title: \\\\\\\"code2vec: Learning Distributed Representations of Code\\\\\\\"\\\\n        authors: \\\\\\\"Uri Alon, Meital Zilberstein, Omer Levy, Eran Yahav\\\\\\\"\\\\n        venue: POPL\\\\n        year: 2019\\\\n        relation: background\\\\n        summary: \\\\\\\"用 AST path 学习代码向量表示，首次大规模证明结构信息对代码表示学习的价值。\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n      - title: \\\\\\\"code2seq: Generating Sequences from Structured Representations of Code\\\\\\\"\\\\n        authors: \\\\\\\"Uri Alon, Shaked Brody, Omer Levy, Eran Yahav\\\\\\\"\\\\n        venue: ICLR\\\\n        year: 2019\\\\n        relation: background\\\\n        summary: \\\\\\\"code2vec 的序列生成扩展，用 AST path attention 生成方法名摘要。\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n      - title: \\\\\\\"Detecting Code Clones with Graph Neural Network and Flow-Augmented Abstract Syntax Tree\\\\\\\"\\\\n        authors: \\\\\\\"Wenhan Wang, Ge Li, Bo Ma, Xin Xia, Zhi Jin\\\\\\\"\\\\n        venue: SANER\\\\n        year: 2020\\\\n        relation: background\\\\n        summary: \\\\\\\"用 data-flow 增强 AST 进行代码克隆检测，与 StructFuse 用 data-flow 做 hard negative 挖掘思路相关。\\\\\\\"\\\\n        note: \\\\\\\"需验证作者和 venue\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n      - title: \\\\\\\"GraphCodeBERT: Pre-training Code Representations with Data Flow\\\\\\\"\\\\n        authors: \\\\\\\"Daya Guo, Shuo Ren, Shuai Lu, Zhangyin Feng, Duyu Tang, Shujie Liu, Long Zhou, Nan Duan, Alexey Svyatkovskiy, Shengyu Fu, Michele Tufano, Shao Kun Deng, Colin Clement, Dawn Drain, Neel Sundaresan, Jian Yin, Daxin Jiang, Ming Zhou\\\\\\\"\\\\n        venue: ICLR\\\\n        year: 2021\\\\n        relation: background\\\\n        summary: \\\\\\\"在预训练中引入 data-flow edge，证明 data-flow 信息提升代码理解任务。StructFuse 的 insight 与此相关但用途不同（hard negative mining vs pre-training）。\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  # ==========================================================================\\\\n  # Category 4: Code Embeddings / Code Search\\\\n  # ==========================================================================\\\\n  code_embeddings_search:\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"代码嵌入模型和代码搜索方法\\\\\\\"\\\\n    papers:\\\\n\\\\n      - title: \\\\\\\"CodeSearchNet Challenge: Evaluating the State of Semantic Code Search\\\\\\\"\\\\n        authors: \\\\\\\"Hamel Husain, Ho-Hsiang Wu, Tiferet Gazit, Miltiadis Allamanis, Marc Brockschmidt\\\\\\\"\\\\n        venue: arXiv\\\\n        year: 2019\\\\n        relation: background\\\\n        summary: \\\\\\\"代码语义搜索 benchmark 和数据集，推动了代码嵌入模型的发展。\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n      - title: \\\\\\\"CodeBERT: A Pre-Trained Model for Programming and Natural Languages\\\\\\\"\\\\n        authors: \\\\\\\"Zhangyin Feng, Daya Guo, Duyu Tang, Nan Duan, Xiaocheng Feng, Ming Gong, Lixin Zou, Bing Qin, Ting Liu, Daxin Jiang, Ming Zhou\\\\\\\"\\\\n        venue: EMNLP (Findings)\\\\n        year: 2020\\\\n        relation: background\\\\n        summary: \\\\\\\"首个编程语言-自然语言双模态预训练模型，代码嵌入的早期里程碑。\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n      - title: \\\\\\\"UniXcoder: Unified Cross-Modal Pre-training for Code Representation\\\\\\\"\\\\n        authors: \\\\\\\"Daya Guo, Shuai Lu, Nan Duan, Yanlin Wang, Ming Zhou, Jian Yin\\\\\\\"\\\\n        venue: ACL\\\\n        year: 2022\\\\n        relation: background\\\\n        summary: \\\\\\\"统一跨模态代码预训练，在代码搜索等任务上取得 SOTA。\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n      - title: \\\\\\\"StarCoder: May the Source Be with You!\\\\\\\"\\\\n        authors: \\\\\\\"Raymond Li, Loubna Ben Allal, et al. (BigCode)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        venue: TMLR\\\\n        year: 2023\\\\n        relation: background\\\\n        summary: \\\\\\\"大规模开源代码 LLM，广泛用于代码嵌入的 backbone。\\\\\\\"\\\\n        note: \\\\\\\"需验证 venue（可能是 arXiv 或其他）\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n      - title: \\\\\\\"Code Llama: Open Foundation Models for Code\\\\\\\"\\\\n        authors: \\\\\\\"Baptiste Rozière, Jonas Gehring, Fabian Gloeckle, et al. (Meta AI)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        venue: arXiv\\\\n        year: 2023\\\\n        relation: background\\\\n        summary: \\\\\\\"Meta 的代码大模型系列，基于 Llama 2 微调。\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n      - title: \\\\\\\"Qwen2.5-Coder Technical Report\\\\\\\"\\\\n        authors: \\\\\\\"Qwen Team (Alibaba)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        venue: arXiv\\\\n        year: 2024\\\\n        relation: building-block  # StructFuse 用 Qwen2.5-Coder-3B 做检索器\\\\n        summary: \\\\\\\"Qwen 代码模型系列，StructFuse 用 Qwen2.5-Coder-3B 作为对比学习检索器的 backbone。\\\\\\\"\\\\n        note: \\\\\\\"需验证确切标题和年份\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n      - title: \\\\\\\"Contrastive Learning for Source Code with Structural and Functional Properties\\\\\\\"\\\\n        authors: \\\\\\\"Yangruibo Ding, Luca Buratti, Saurabh Pujar, Alessandro Morari, Baishakhi Ray, Saikat Chakraborty\\\\\\\"\\\\n        venue: ACL (Findings)\\\\n        year: 2022\\\\n        relation: background\\\\n        summary: \\\\\\\"代码对比学习中利用结构/功能属性构建正负样本对。\\\\\\\"\\\\n        note: \\\\\\\"需验证作者和 venue\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n      - title: \\\\\\\"BM25\\\\\\\"\\\\n        authors: \\\\\\\"Stephen Robertson, Hugo Zaragoza\\\\\\\"\\\\n        venue: \\\\\\\"Foundations and Trends in Information Retrieval\\\\\\\"\\\\n        year: 2009\\\\n        relation: baseline\\\\n        summary: \\\\\\\"经典稀疏检索方法，StructFuse 的 baseline 之一。Phase 2a 实验发现 BM25 在 bug fixing 定位中可能有误导性（负系数）。\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n# ==========================================================================\\\\n# 待补充\\\\n# ==========================================================================\\\\n# 以下论文可能相关，待确认后补充：\\\\n# - FAISS (Johnson et al., 2019) — ANN 检索库，StructFuse 评估可能用到\\\\n# - Tree-sitter — 增量解析器，与 CodeQL 互补\\\\n# - Aider / Moatless Tools — SWE-bench 上的其他代码检索方法\\\\n# - CoSQA (Huang et al., 2021) — 代码搜索 QA 数据集\\\\n# - DeepSeek-Coder — 另一个可能的 backbone 对比\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 9647, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XZwZskh51fHaXwMmZ5Pp6f","session_id":"1a45356f-658c-4c4f-ba94-f04e8cd4eef3","uuid":"22e45e60-4323-40a2-863b-6bfb8de189c1","timestamp":"2026-05-14T17:08:18.214Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Tx8b81YfFCgxauUa42uEGd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013HdZQquQEbhVVLF2oq99uF","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R2: Novelty + Related Work review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R2 for a top ML venue review. Your focus areas are **Novelty** and **Related Work**. Use a 6-point scale (1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept). Target acceptance rate ~25%.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\nTitle: \"What Makes Hard Negatives Work for Code Retrieval? A Systematic Study of Mining Strategies and Representation Geometry\"\n\nThis is a **systematic empirical study** (self-described analysis paper) comparing 4 hard negative mining strategies for contrastive code retrieval:\n- **Random**: uniform sampling of non-gold files\n- **BM25-Proxy**: top-K by BM25 score (what CoCoHaNeRe called \"embedding-distance\" negatives)\n- **Embedding-Distance**: true dense embedding nearest neighbors\n- **Dataflow-Disconnected**: structurally disconnected files via CodeQL inter-procedural analysis\n\nSetup: 2 decoder-only encoders (Qwen2.5-Coder-3B, StarCoder2-3B), SWE-smith training data (5K instances), pool=50, LoRA, 3 seeds, InfoNCE τ=0.05.\n\nBenchmarks: SWE-smith validation, RepoBench-R, SWE-bench Lite (300 instances).\n\n## Key Claims and Findings\n\n1. **Embedding mining tends to help** (+0.5-1.0pp R@1) — direction consistent across encoders, benchmarks, seeds, hyperparameters. But effect sizes modest, multi-seed CIs 2-4pp wide, some seed-level deltas < 0.5pp.\n\n2. **BM25-proxy negatives trend toward harm** (−0.7 to −0.9pp), providing partial correction to CoCoHaNeRe's −27pp claim. But: our BM25 effect is not statistically significant (p=0.12, p=0.18), and the magnitude gap (−1.9pp vs −27pp) is large. Paper argues CoCoHaNeRe conflated BM25-proxy with true embedding negatives.\n\n3. **Dataflow is an exploratory observation**: marginal positive on Qwen, negative on StarCoder. Encoder-strategy interaction. CI includes 0 in most conditions. Structural data only available for 34% of instances.\n\n4. **Stratified analysis**: Mining benefit concentrates in small repos, hard negatives, medium query-positive similarity. These favorable conditions are a minority of real-world distribution.\n\n5. **Pool size sensitivity**: Embedding advantage shrinks from +1.0pp (pool=50) to +0.5pp (pool=500). Real-world pools are 200-1000+.\n\n## Related Work Coverage in Paper\n\nThe paper covers three areas:\n- **Hard Negative Mining for Dense Retrieval**: DPR (Karpukhin 2020), ANCE (Xiong 2021), curriculum-based approaches, CoCoHaNeRe. Only 2 citations in this paragraph.\n- **Code Retrieval for Software Engineering**: SweRank, SWE-Fixer mentioned briefly.\n- **Structure-Aware Code Intelligence**: GraphCodeBERT, CodexGraph, LocAgent, RANGER, ARISE mentioned. Table 20 compares with inference-time methods.\n\nOnly 2 references in the full paper (Karpukhin 2020, Xiong 2021).\n\n## Experiment Design Reference\n\nThe review_context.yaml specifies the narrative guidance: Claims downgraded to \"tends to help\" and \"exploratory observation.\" Paper positioned as \"Systematic Study\" / analysis paper. SWE-bench delta < 1pp, not independent evidence. The CoCoHaNeRe correction argument softened from \"we prove wrong\" to \"directional support for proxy conflation hypothesis.\"\n\nThe inference-time graph comparison (plan_017) is analysis-only (no experiment), noting complementarity is speculative.\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nWrite a detailed review covering:\n\n1. **Summary** (2-3 sentences)\n2. **Strengths** (bullet points)\n3. **Weaknesses** (bullet points)\n4. **Questions for authors** (numbered)\n5. **Minor issues**\n6. **Overall assessment** with score and confidence\n\nFocus specifically on:\n- **Novelty**: Is the research question worth asking? Is the systematic comparison itself a contribution? Does the dataflow-grounded negative strategy represent genuine methodological novelty?\n- **Related work depth and fairness**: Is the coverage adequate? Are there critical missing references? The paper only cites 2 works — is this sufficient?\n- **Positioning**: Is \"analysis paper\" the right framing? Does the paper deliver enough insight to justify publication at a top venue without a strong method contribution?\n- **CoCoHaNeRe correction argument**: Is it properly substantiated? The paper claims CoCoHaNeRe conflated BM25-proxy with true embedding negatives — but the evidence is directional, not conclusive.\n- **Broader impact and significance**: Would this paper change how practitioners or researchers think about hard negatives for code retrieval?\n- **Writing quality and presentation**: Is the paper clearly written? Are claims properly hedged?\n\nEvaluate whether this analysis paper meets the bar for a top venue. Analysis papers can be valuable, but they need to deliver substantial new understanding. Assess whether this paper does that given the modest effect sizes and wide confidence intervals."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34254,"cache_read_input_tokens":22925,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":34254},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a45356f-658c-4c4f-ba94-f04e8cd4eef3","uuid":"9a5511ea-e9c6-48ca-84bc-53e1ab6c6cdd"}
